solutions.latex:
The diagram shows a possible graph of $y = f(x)$.

\exfigure{1310_q10_s1}

The graph of $y = -f(x)$ will be a reflection in the $x$-axis producing a maximum turning point at $(-4, 6)$.

The dilation experienced by $y = -f(2x)$ will halve the distance of all points on $y = -f(x)$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the maximum turning point at $(-4, 6)$ on the graph of $y = -f(x)$ will move to $(-2, 6)$ on the graph of $y = -f(2x)$.

